2.1 Purpose and Scope
This phase fixes exactly what ComicCraft must do before code is written, so every requirement traces to a module and a test case.

In scope for v1: one comic per request, five panels, one browser session, local deployment, PDF export.

Out of scope for v1: user accounts, saved comic libraries, multi-page arcs, cloud deployment, collaborative editing.

2.2 Stakeholders
Stakeholder	Interest
Casual user / non-artist	Wants a finished comic from a one-line idea without drawing skill
Storyteller / hobbyist	Wants to iterate on tone and art style until it matches their vision
API consumer	Wants programmatic generation via structured JSON
Developer / maintainer	Wants swappable models and isolated per-stage failure
