2.6 Assumptions and Dependencies
Gemini API key with quota for at least two calls per comic (Flash + Pro).
PyTorch-capable hardware for Stable Diffusion; CPU inference works but is slow.
Diffusers and runwayml/stable-diffusion-v1-5 weights downloadable at first run.
Python 3.10+, FastAPI, Uvicorn, Jinja2, FPDF, Pillow, python-multipart, python-dotenv.
2.7 Constraints
Latency floor — five sequential diffusion calls set the minimum wait.
No persistence — a refresh loses the comic.
Single comic per request — no multi-chapter support.
Local-only — no auth layer, so the JSON route must not be exposed publicly as-is.
2.8 Acceptance Criteria
A user submits the fox/enchanted-forest prompt with tone dramatic and style anime and receives five distinct panels with readable narration; resubmitting as funny + comic book produces a visibly different comic; download yields a timestamped PDF with one panel per page and lands on the success page; a forced single-panel failure still returns the remaining four.
